  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sustainable management and conservation of wetlands and grasslands in the Son Kul Lake</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This activity focuses on the sustainable management and conservation of wetlands and grasslands in the Son Kul Lake pilot area in Kyrgyzstan. It aims to strengthen the capacity of local communities and civil society actors to protect ecosystems, promote biodiversity conservation, and support climate-resilient livelihoods. The activity combines participatory environmental management, awareness-raising, and practical conservation measures, with a strong focus on inclusive local engagement, improved knowledge of sustainable land use, and long-term stewardship of natural resources.</narrative>
  </description>
